Dante obtained the Amulet of Elf King Oberon sometime after the defeat of [[the Professor]] and prior to the discovery of the [[Nexus]] in [[Peru]]. Oberon was invoked alongside [[Zhalia Moon|Zhalia Moon's]] [[Gar-Ghoul]] to fight against three [[Gigadrone]] Titans summoned by the new [[Organization]] team led by [[Wilder]]. He attacked [[Dark Dryad]] and knocked her back, but she entangled him in vines to allow his defeat by [[Myrmidon]]. {{Source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Dante's Elf King Oberon was invoked to fight against [[Kiel]]'s [[Balenpyre]] outside the [[Pyramid of the Sun]] in Mexico. After a fierce battle, the two Titans sent each other back to their [[Amulets]]. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

On the island of the [[Phoenix]], Oberon was used to release a pile of logs on a [[Casterwill Hunter]] and a [[Harlekin]] which rolled over them. Oberon quickly finished off the escaping and now quite angry Harlekin. {{source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

At the tomb [[Nostradamus]], Oberon was used alongside [[Den Fears|Den Fears']] [[Dullahan]] to battle [[Marduk|Marduk's]] [[Psikofen]] and to buy Dante the time he needed to locate the [[Spiral Mark]]. After kicking Psikofen down the steps of the tomb, Oberon was then demobilized by Psikofen's chains before defeating Marduk's [[Helinx]] Titan.{{source|Words from Eathon}}
